IMPORT prelude

-- Exchanges (Demutualisation and Merger) Act 1999 (Singapore) -- what the 1999 demutualisation of SES, SIMEX and SCCS gave the
-- old members and seat-holders (s 6), the share cancellation and re-creation and the 30-day notice (ss 3(1), 4, 5), the
-- statutory requirements the offer and issue of the holding company's shares escape (ss 4(5), 8(3), 8(4), 9), what the special
-- purpose company may and may not do with its shares and their proceeds (ss 8(1A), 10, 11), and the deemed Trustees Act
-- track record of the holding company (s 12).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 21/3/2022 to 20/10/2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/EDMA1999.txt. The revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December
-- 2021"; the latest amendment annotated in the body is Act 4 of 2022 wef 21/03/2022 (ss 8(1A), 8(2), 8(5), 10(2), 11, and the
-- repeal of s 13). THE ARRANGEMENT OF SECTIONS IN THE DEPOSIT IS ONE LINE OUT OF STEP with the body (it lists "2. Short title",
-- "3. Interpretation" and so on); this encoding follows the body's numbering (s 1 short title, s 2 interpretation, s 3 transfer
-- date ... s 12 Trustees Act, s 13 repealed).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0112 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has
-- asked a sharper question yet. The Act is a one-off transitional statute: almost everything it decides happened on the transfer
-- date, 1 December 1999. What it still decides for a person is (a) what a former SES or SIMEX shareholder or SIMEX seat-holder
-- was entitled to, (b) the continuing restrictions on the special purpose company's holding, and (c) whether a trustee could
-- treat the holding company's securities as an authorised investment.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: the recitals; the definitions (s 2) beyond their use here; the Minister's designations (s 3(2)); the transfer of
-- reserves and assets (s 7); the Minister's choice of share value (s 6(5)(a)) and the single offer to the special purpose company
-- (s 8(1)), beyond taking their figures as inputs; the Take-over Code itself; the conditions of the old Trustees Act Schedule
-- other than the three that s 12 deems satisfied. No Gazette notification, Minister's notice or later Trustees Act text was
-- retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Exchanges (Demutualisation and Merger) Act 1999`

GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` MEANS
    IF `a` AT LEAST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

§§ `6 -- what the old members and seat-holders received`

-- s 6(1): the transferee holding company "must, on the transfer date, allot and issue to SES shareholders as at the transfer date
-- such number of new transferee holding company's shares as amounting to $6 million in value for each SES share, with the
-- exception of the SES shares held by any SES shareholder in involuntary liquidation as at 4 November 1998 including Associated
-- Asian Securities (Pte) Limited (in liquidation)".
-- s 6(3)(a): to SIMEX shareholders, "$115,000 in value for each SIMEX share", with the same involuntary-liquidation exception;
-- (b): "to registered owners of SIMEX seats as at the transfer date ... $170,000 in value for each SIMEX seat" -- with NO
-- liquidation exception.
-- s 6(2), (4): "No fraction of a new transferee holding company's share may be allotted or issued".
-- s 6(5): the shares are "of such value as the Minister may, by notification in the Gazette, determine" and issued as fully paid.
DECLARE Member HAS
    `SES shares held on the transfer date` IS A NUMBER
    `SIMEX shares held on the transfer date` IS A NUMBER
    `SIMEX seats registered on the transfer date` IS A NUMBER
    `in involuntary liquidation as at 4 November 1998` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the member` IS A Member
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the value of holding company shares due` MEANS
    IF `the member`'s `in involuntary liquidation as at 4 November 1998`
    THEN `the member`'s `SIMEX seats registered on the transfer date` TIMES 170000
    ELSE    `the member`'s `SES shares held on the transfer date` TIMES 6000000
        PLUS `the member`'s `SIMEX shares held on the transfer date` TIMES 115000
        PLUS `the member`'s `SIMEX seats registered on the transfer date` TIMES 170000

-- Whole shares only. The text says no fraction may be allotted but not whether the count is rounded down; reading it as the
-- largest whole number of shares whose value does not exceed the entitlement is an INFERENCE from "amounting to".
GIVEN `the entitlement` IS A NUMBER, `the value of one share` IS A NUMBER, `the number allotted` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the allotment fits section 6` IF
        `the number allotted` TIMES `the value of one share` AT MOST `the entitlement`
    AND (`the number allotted` PLUS 1) TIMES `the value of one share` GREATER THAN `the entitlement`

§§ `3(1), 4 and 5 -- cancellation, re-creation and notice`

-- s 3(1): "The transfer date is 1 December 1999."
-- s 4(1)-(3): on the transfer date the capital is reduced by cancelling all issued shares, "which are 34 SES shares", "40 SIMEX
-- shares", "34 SCCS shares". (4): every share certificate is "deemed to be cancelled" and "ceases ... to have effect as a document
-- of title". (5): the reduction "is not subject to the requirements of section 73 of the Companies Act" (special resolution).
-- s 5(1)-(3): capital is then increased "to $34 by the creation of 34 SES shares", "to $40 by the creation of 40 SIMEX shares" and
-- "to $34 by the creation of 34 SCCS shares", all issued fully paid to the transferee holding company.
-- s 5(4): the transferee holding company "must, within 30 days of the transfer date, give a notice to the Registrar of Companies".
DECLARE Exchange IS ONE OF
    SES
    SIMEX
    SCCS

GIVEN `the exchange` IS AN Exchange
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the shares cancelled and re-created` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the exchange`
    WHEN SES THEN 34
    WHEN SIMEX THEN 40
    WHEN SCCS THEN 34

GIVEN `the exchange` IS AN Exchange
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the capital in dollars after re-creation` MEANS
    `the shares cancelled and re-created` `the exchange`

GIVEN `held immediately before the transfer date` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an old certificate is still a document of title` IF
    FALSE

-- Day 0 is 1 December 1999. Counting day 30 (31 December 1999) as "within 30 days" is an INFERENCE.
GIVEN `days after the transfer date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice to the Registrar is in time` IF
    `days after the transfer date` AT MOST 30

§§ `4(5), 8(3), 8(4), 9 -- requirements disapplied`

-- s 4(5): no special resolution under s 73 Companies Act for the s 4 reduction.
-- s 8(3): the prospectus requirements of the Securities and Futures Act 2001 do "not apply to an offer of shares made by the
-- transferee holding company under subsection (1) or by the special purpose company under subsection (2)".
-- s 8(4): s 76 Companies Act ("prohibits a company from financing dealings in its own shares") does not apply to any guarantee,
-- indemnity, warranty, representation or other undertaking in relation to an offer under (1) or (2).
-- s 9: s 59 Companies Act (statement in lieu of a prospectus) "does not apply to the issue of the transferee holding company's
-- shares under section 6 or 8".
DECLARE Requirement IS ONE OF
    `special resolution for reducing capital`
    `SFA prospectus requirements`
    `ban on financing dealings in own shares`
    `statement in lieu of prospectus`

DECLARE Transaction IS ONE OF
    `the s 4 capital reduction`
    `the s 6 allotment to members`
    `the single offer to the special purpose company`
    `a sale by the special purpose company on the Minister's direction`
    `a later share issue by the holding company outside the Act`

GIVEN `the requirement` IS A Requirement, `the transaction` IS A Transaction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act disapplies the requirement` IF
    CONSIDER `the requirement`
    WHEN `special resolution for reducing capital` THEN `the transaction` EQUALS `the s 4 capital reduction`
    WHEN `SFA prospectus requirements` THEN
            `the transaction` EQUALS `the single offer to the special purpose company`
        OR  `the transaction` EQUALS `a sale by the special purpose company on the Minister's direction`
    WHEN `ban on financing dealings in own shares` THEN
            `the transaction` EQUALS `the single offer to the special purpose company`
        OR  `the transaction` EQUALS `a sale by the special purpose company on the Minister's direction`
    WHEN `statement in lieu of prospectus` THEN
            `the transaction` EQUALS `the s 6 allotment to members`
        OR  `the transaction` EQUALS `the single offer to the special purpose company`
        OR  `the transaction` EQUALS `a sale by the special purpose company on the Minister's direction`

§§ `8(1A), 8(2), 11(2) -- what the special purpose company may do`

-- s 8(1A): "with the Minister's approval" it may (a) subscribe to any rights issue; (b) elect to receive scrip dividends; (c) take
-- part in any other corporate action under which it may opt to receive additional shares.
-- s 8(2): it "must, from time to time, offer for sale" such shares "at such price and on such terms, as the Minister may, by
-- written notice, direct".
-- s 11(2): despite the Companies Act and its constitution it must (a) hold the shares "for the benefit of the Financial Sector
-- Development Fund"; (b) "not exercise or control the exercise of the votes attached to such shares"; (c) not dispose of, deal
-- with or create security interests over them "without the prior approval of the Minister or as otherwise permitted under this
-- Act"; (d) hold any dividend or distribution for the benefit of the Fund.
-- Voting is barred outright: no Minister's approval lifts (b).
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    `vote the shares`
    `sell on the Minister's s 8(2) direction`
    `sell on its own initiative`
    `charge the shares as security`
    `subscribe to a rights issue`
    `elect scrip dividends`
    `keep a dividend for itself`

GIVEN `the action` IS AN Action, `the Minister approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the special purpose company may take the action` IF
    CONSIDER `the action`
    WHEN `vote the shares` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `sell on the Minister's s 8(2) direction` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sell on its own initiative` THEN `the Minister approved`
    WHEN `charge the shares as security` THEN `the Minister approved`
    WHEN `subscribe to a rights issue` THEN `the Minister approved`
    WHEN `elect scrip dividends` THEN `the Minister approved`
    WHEN `keep a dividend for itself` THEN FALSE

§§ `11(1) -- take-over thresholds`

-- s 11(1): despite ss 139, 140 of the Securities and Futures Act 2001 and the Take-over Code, the shares held by the special
-- purpose company "which it acquired under section 8(1) or (1A) are not to be taken into account" in deciding whether it, a
-- related company, or a company acting in concert, has acquired voting shares for those provisions.
-- That shares acquired in some other way still count is an INFERENCE from the words "which it acquired under section 8(1) or (1A)".
DECLARE Acquisition IS ONE OF
    `the single offer under s 8(1)`
    `a Minister-approved corporate action under s 8(1A)`
    `a purchase in the market`

GIVEN `how acquired` IS AN Acquisition
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the shares count towards a take-over threshold` IF
    `how acquired` EQUALS `a purchase in the market`

§§ `10 -- proceeds of sale`

-- s 10(1): the Authority "is authorised to utilise the proceeds" of s 8(2) sales "to meet the expenses and fees associated with"
-- the demutualisation and merger, the formation of the two companies and the offer and sale. (2): "The remainder of the proceeds
-- ... must be paid by the special purpose company into the Financial Sector Development Fund."
-- The Act does not say what happens if expenses exceed proceeds; a remainder of nil is an INFERENCE.
GIVEN `the proceeds` IS A NUMBER, `the expenses and fees met` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount payable into the Fund` MEANS
    `the greater of` (`the proceeds` MINUS `the expenses and fees met`) 0

§§ `12 -- deemed track record for trustees`

-- s 12(1): for applying paragraph 1(1)(b), (c) and (d) of Part IV of the First Schedule to the Trustees Act 1967 "as in force
-- immediately before 15 December 2004" (a company's securities are authorised investments only if it has "shareholders equity of
-- not less than $30 million", "has paid dividends in each of the relevant 3 years", and "has reported a profit in the financial
-- year immediately preceding that in which the investment is made"), the transferee holding company is deemed --
-- (a) to have paid a dividend in each financial year preceding the first investment year that is in the relevant 3 years, and in
-- the first investment year "if that year is included in the relevant 3 years and the transferee holding company does not in fact
-- pay such a dividend in that year"; (b) to have shareholders equity of not less than $30 million; (c) to have reported a profit
-- in the financial year preceding the first investment year, and in the first investment year if it does not in fact.
-- (2): "the relevant 3 years" are the 3 financial years immediately preceding the year of the investment.
-- The "first investment year" is the financial year in which the transfer date falls. Years are counted here from it: year 0 is the
-- first investment year, year -1 the one before, year 1 the one after. The deeming runs out: an investment in year 2 needs a real
-- dividend and a real profit in year 1, and one in year 4 needs real dividends in years 1 to 3.
DECLARE `Actual Results` HAS
    `paid a dividend in year 1` IS A BOOLEAN
    `paid a dividend in year 2` IS A BOOLEAN
    `paid a dividend in year 3` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reported a profit in year 1` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reported a profit in year 2` IS A BOOLEAN
    `reported a profit in year 3` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the results` IS AN `Actual Results`, `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a dividend counts for the year` IF
    IF `the year` AT MOST 0 THEN TRUE
    ELSE IF `the year` EQUALS 1 THEN `the results`'s `paid a dividend in year 1`
        ELSE IF `the year` EQUALS 2 THEN `the results`'s `paid a dividend in year 2`
            ELSE IF `the year` EQUALS 3 THEN `the results`'s `paid a dividend in year 3`
                ELSE FALSE

GIVEN `the results` IS AN `Actual Results`, `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a profit counts for the year` IF
    IF `the year` AT MOST 0 THEN TRUE
    ELSE IF `the year` EQUALS 1 THEN `the results`'s `reported a profit in year 1`
        ELSE IF `the year` EQUALS 2 THEN `the results`'s `reported a profit in year 2`
            ELSE IF `the year` EQUALS 3 THEN `the results`'s `reported a profit in year 3`
                ELSE FALSE

-- Only the three deemed conditions (b), (c), (d) are modelled; equity of $30 million is always deemed under s 12(1)(b). Years
-- before year -1 are deemed for dividends by (a) and never need a profit, so "AT MOST 0" covers them. The model is meant for
-- investments in years 0 to 4.
GIVEN `the results` IS AN `Actual Results`, `the investment year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deemed and actual record meets paragraphs 1(1)(b) to (d)` IF
        `a dividend counts for the year` `the results` (`the investment year` MINUS 3)
    AND `a dividend counts for the year` `the results` (`the investment year` MINUS 2)
    AND `a dividend counts for the year` `the results` (`the investment year` MINUS 1)
    AND `a profit counts for the year` `the results` (`the investment year` MINUS 1)
